The Chinese harness's test sets, made by ../make_sets.py from openly licensed text. None of it is the user's own
words or userdb. Each file keeps its sources' licences (tools/chinese-lm/SOURCES.md has the revisions):

- The chat sets (*-chat.tsv, and the chat items in typo.tsv and variants.tsv): the test documents
  (tools/chinese-lm/common.py's split()) of
  - AliMeeting (OpenSLR 119) and AISHELL-4 (OpenSLR 111): their evaluation and test meetings' transcripts,
    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0, by Alibaba DAMO Academy and AISHELL. The files that hold
    them are therefore CC BY-SA 4.0 as a whole;
  - HundredCV-Chat (Jax-dan), Apache-2.0;
  - Tatoeba's Mandarin sentences, Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 France, by Tatoeba's contributors;
  - KdConv (thu-coai, Zhou et al. 2020), Apache-2.0;
  - OpenAssistant oasst2, Apache-2.0, by the OpenAssistant contributors.
- The news sets (*-news.tsv, and the news items in typo.tsv and variants.tsv): Chinese Wikinews articles
  (https://zh.wikinews.org, the 200 newest published in the dump of 2026-11-01; wikinews-articles.tsv lists
  each one's page id), Creative Commons Attribution 2.5, by Wikinews's contributors.
- The pinyin, abbreviations and typos in every file are generated (MIT, ../../../../LICENSE-SebType).
